To thoroughly test your multi-level workflow (W1_3_APPROVERS and W2_4_APPROVERS), you must satisfy two strict business rules we implemented:
 1. **No Self-Approval:** A Maker cannot approve their own batch.
 2. **No Duplicate Approval:** A Checker cannot approve the same batch at two different levels.
Because of this, you need a minimum of **6 distinct users** to test all possible workflow permutations without hitting security violation errors.
Here is the exact user matrix and the step-by-step SQL commands to create this test data in your Oracle database.
### The Required User Matrix
| User ID | Role Name | Role ID | Purpose in Testing |
|---|---|---|---|
| **TCS_MAKER** | TCSGLIF | 51 | Creates batches to trigger Workflow 1. |
| **TCS_CHECK1** | TCSGLIF | 51 | W1 Level 1 Approver & W2 Level 1 Approver. |
| **TCS_CHECK2** | TCSGLIF | 51 | W2 Level 2 Approver (must be different from CHECK1). |
| **SBI_CHECK1** | SBIGLIF | 52 | W1 Level 2 Approver & W2 Level 3 Approver. |
| **SBI_CHECK2** | SBIGLIF | 52 | Final execution approver for both workflows. |
| **OTHER_MAKER** | OTHER | 53 | Creates batches to trigger Workflow 2. |
### Step-by-Step SQL Script
Execute these commands in your Oracle SQL client (like SQL Developer or DBeaver).
